# libhoudini.so digests.
#
# Written by tools/apply-houdini-patch.sh, read by tools/check-houdini-blob.sh
# and by the build (build.sh calls the checker before it builds the image).
#
# donor   the unmodified Intel blob the patch is applied to
# patched the blob that ships in the image
#
# If the tree holds the donor, the image builds cleanly, boots cleanly and
# then freezes in every game: the patch that gives pool B more than one
# workspace lives in these bytes and nothing else in the build knows about
# it. This happened once already (an image built before the patch was applied
# to the tree), so the check is part of the build, not a manual step.
donor a252c506ea7435d99839f8ae741908f8c19e2d67a445919146128eabe7fee9cb
patched 5c4f83b03b6f5b1159fe19d32a65677e6529b02e866f154d59d28df48da8ec7c
